issue.description:
Polish the Sidebar token controls so the toggle row feels quieter and has clearer spacing from the SIDEBAR collapsible trigger.

Owner direction:

* Make the "Use sidebar tokens" label one text step smaller.
* Use the muted-foreground semantic token for the label color.
* Remove the helper note below the toggle:
  "Sidebar tokens are currently not applied."
* Add a small amount of vertical space above the toggle row so it is visually separated from the SIDEBAR collapsible trigger.

Visual intent:

* Keep the toggle row visually secondary to the actual sidebar token fields.
* Reduce clutter in the section.
* Improve vertical rhythm between the collapsible trigger and the toggle.

Preserve:

* existing Switch behavior;
* existing useDedicatedTokens semantics;
* current enabled/disabled behavior;
* keyboard/focus states;
* light/dark behavior;
* sidebar token field order and values;
* collapsible trigger styling and behavior.

Do not:

* change sidebar token architecture;
* change helper copy elsewhere;
* change token values;
* add new controls;
* alter the SIDEBAR trigger itself beyond the spacing relationship needed below it.

Acceptance:

* "Use sidebar tokens" renders one text step smaller than before.
* The label uses muted-foreground styling.
* The "Sidebar tokens are currently not applied." note is removed.
* There is a small clear gap between the SIDEBAR collapsible trigger and the toggle row.
* Toggle behavior and accessibility remain unchanged.
* No unrelated sidebar control styling changes.
